export const title = "AWS S3 Upload";
export const html = "<h1>AWS S3 Upload</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<p>An action type that lets you upload event snapshots to an AWS S3 bucket when an application event occurs. The path key of the storage location where the snapshot file is saved can be set variably using the event's metadata.</p>\n\n<p>An AWS S3 Upload action can be added from the action settings screen.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>AWS S3</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Setting the action type to <strong>AWS S3</strong> reveals the related settings below it.</p>\n\n<h2>Snapshot Time Range Settings</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:150px 1fr 40px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;align-items:center;\">\n    <span>Snapshot Time Range</span><input value=\"-2\" disabled style=\"width:60px;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;\">~</span><span><input value=\"1\" disabled style=\"width:60px;\"> second(s)</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Sets the time range of upload snapshots based on the event time. With the example setting above, snapshots generated from 2 seconds before the event to 1 second after the event are uploaded.</p>\n<p>Separately from event-time snapshots, periodic snapshots are generated for each channel at a minimum rate of 1 per second.</p>\n\n<h2>File Path Settings</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr 60px;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>File Path</span><input value=\"{{TIME YYYYMMDD}}/{{TIME HHMMSS}}\" disabled><span>.jpg</span>\n    <span>Example</span><span style=\"grid-column:span 2;font-family:monospace;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--text-muted);\">20220902/153702.jpg</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>File path setting, with a token example</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p>The file path sets the path where the snapshot image is stored.</p>\n<p>The setting can include event metadata. If you include time-related metadata in the path setting as in the example above, the upload file path is set based on the time the event occurred.</p>\n<p>The file path setting only covers the path within the bucket &ndash; you don't need to include the Region or Bucket in it.</p>\n<p>Once you've set the file path, the Example field shows a preview of the snapshot's path.</p>\n\n<h2>AWS S3 Storage Settings</h2>\n<p>Add the AWS S3 storage settings under the Server item.</p>\n<p>Once added, an AWS S3 storage setting can be used when configuring other rules or when setting up AWS S3 Upload actions in other apps.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:120px;\"><span class=\"btn small primary\">+ Add</span></div>\n<p>Click the Add button to add a new server setting.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\" style=\"max-width:420px;margin:0 auto;\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">AWS S3</div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n      <span>Name</span><input value=\"My Seoul Event Bucket\" disabled>\n      <span>Region</span><select disabled><option>Asia Pacific (Seoul)</option></select>\n      <span>Bucket</span><input value=\"mycompany.event.seoul\" disabled>\n      <span>Access Key</span><input value=\"AKIA43J3I7YRCPWUX3HF\" disabled>\n      <span>Secret Key</span><input value=\"&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;\" disabled>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"modal-foot\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Apply</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>AWS S3 storage configuration</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p>Enter the target AWS S3 storage information and click the <strong>Apply</strong> button to apply the settings.</p>\n<p>Once an AWS S3 storage setting is added, a new item appears in the server list.</p>\n<p>Check the target item in the list to complete the AWS S3 storage setting.</p>";
